{
  "_comment": [
    "Pinned third-party JavaScript, committed to the repo instead of loaded from a CDN.",
    "Rationale: keeps the CSP at script-src 'self' (no widening), and stops a third party",
    "from learning that a user opened a PDF. The cost is that these files do NOT update",
    "themselves \u2014 they parse untrusted input, so they must be reviewed on a schedule.",
    "Verify with:  python3 tools/verify_vendor.py",
    "Update with:  see DEVELOPMENT.md -> 'Dipendenze vendorizzate'"
  ],
